instruction:
Work in the Go repo at /gin (module github.com/gin-gonic/gin). TASK: find and FIX TWO bugs in /gin/context.go. Both are in the same file, so fix both in one pass.

BUG A (already diagnosed for you): the hidden test `TestContextRenderAndEscapeAttachment` must pass. In `/gin/context.go`, the method `FileAttachment(filepath, filename string)` builds the Content-Disposition header. Current code:
```go
func (c *Context) FileAttachment(filepath, filename string) {
	if isASCII(filename) {
		c.Writer.Header().Set("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="`+filename+`"`)
	} else {
		c.Writer.Header().Set("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''`+url.QueryEscape(filename))
	}
	http.ServeFile(c.Writer, c.Request, filepath)
}
```
The bug: in the ASCII branch the filename is interpolated into a quoted string without escaping `"` and `\`, so a filename containing a double quote produces a malformed/injectable header. FIX: add a package-level helper (e.g. `var quoteEscaper = strings.NewReplacer("\\", "\\\\", "\"", "\\\"")` and `func escapeQuotes(s string) string { return quoteEscaper.Replace(s) }`) and use `escapeQuotes(filename)` in the ASCII branch. Add the `strings` import if needed (check existing imports first). The existing tests TestContextRenderAttachment and TestContextRenderUTF8Attachment must still pass.

BUG B: the hidden test `TestContextNegotiationFormat2` must pass. Expected behaviour: `Context.NegotiateFormat(offered ...string) string` (and the `negotiate` helper) must correctly implement HTTP content negotiation over the request's `Accept` header: it must pick the best matching offered format, handle `*/*`, handle `type/*`, handle q-values/ordering, and return "" when nothing matches. Read `NegotiateFormat`, `negotiate`, and the `accept`/`accepted` parsing helpers in context.go, and the file's comments. Find the bug (e.g. wrong comparison, wrong handling of the `*` wildcard, wrong q-value parsing, wrong return value when no match) and fix it minimally. Check the existing tests TestContextNegotiationFormat and TestContextNegotiationFormatWithAccept in context_test.go and make sure they still pass.

Verify with `cd /gin && go build ./... && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40` and `go test -run 'Negotiat|Attachment' -v . 2>&1 | tail -80`. CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS: do NOT modify or delete any existing test file; do NOT break any pre-existing passing test; make the smallest possible edits; leave no extra files behind. Report: the exact diff (git diff), test output, and confirmation that `go test ./...` passes.
